Not clean. The core C1–C7 algebra survives the hostile checks, but two exported absorption claims are not justified at their stated scope.

### G1 — The zero-lift correction was not propagated into the A3 pin

A3 asserts unconditionally:

> \[
> dv_1(\widehat k_t)=M_t.
> \]

But r4 explicitly establishes:

> \[
> \operatorname{lift}_i(0;m)=0,
> \qquad
> dv_i(0)=+\infty.
> \]

Only \(c_0\ne0\) is assumed; coefficients \(c_t\) for \(t>0\) may vanish. When \(c_t=0\),

\[
\Gamma_t=c_t\eta^{W(t)}=0,\qquad
\widehat k_t=L_{M_t}(0)=0,
\]

so \(dv_1(\widehat k_t)=+\infty\), not \(M_t\). Therefore the displayed A3 consumption implication is false for an allowed coefficient slot.

The same scope tension appears in A6’s unqualified phrase “with its full displayed support and exact height,” although C6 supplies exact height only for \(\lambda\ne0\).

Classification: GAP — false exported pin on the allowed zero-coefficient branch.

### G2 — The A2 carry derivation silently requires a binary second-level carry

The imported interface states only

> \[
> w_2=\left\lfloor\frac{s(k)+s(k')}{e_2}\right\rfloor,
> \qquad
> m(k+k')=m(k)+m(k')+w_2u_2.
> \]

It does not state \(0\le s(k)<e_2\), or equivalently \(w_2\in\{0,1\}\). Nevertheless the proof claims that two uses of C5-carry yield

\[
Q(m+m'+w_2u_2)-Q(m)-Q(m')
=
\operatorname{wrap}_1(m,m')
+w_2\!\left(Q(u_2)+\operatorname{wrap}_1(m+m',u_2)\right).
\]

That formula follows from C5-carry only when \(w_2=0\) or \(1\). For larger \(w_2\), successive additions of \(u_2\) generally have different wrap terms.

For example, take \(e_1=2,h=1,i_0=1\), so \(q(n)=\lfloor n/2\rfloor\), and let

\[
m=m'=0,\qquad u_2=1,\qquad w_2=2.
\]

These values are not excluded by the displayed supplier interface. The left side is \(q(2)=1\), while the claimed right side is \(0\). Thus the third pinned HETOW display is not a consequence of the named interface plus C5 as written.

Classification: GAP — the re-scoped A2 implication lacks a supplier fact used essentially by its proof.

The positive wrap sign, \(\Theta=\vartheta^{-1}\), canonical \(w\)-twist, \(-q(k)\) sign, \(z^\nu\) bridge, general-stage height typing, and C7 weld fences otherwise remain mutually consistent.

VERDICT: FINDINGS | FINDINGS: 0C + 2G + 0m
